Date: Thu, 3 Sep 2026 18:20:01 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 09/10] .22 Alpaca Paper Execution Adapter: accept the full
 discovered coin universe

This is the actual order-submission allowlist gate, so this change is
called out separately from the .13-.19/.23 report-layer changes: it
directly affects what this adapter will submit to Alpaca's paper API.

Replaces the fixed {"BTC/USD", "ETH/USD"} REQUIRED_SYMBOLS allowlist in
validate_spec() with SUPPORTED_SYMBOL_PATTERN, a structural check
(^[A-Z0-9]{2,10}/USD$) matching the exact same USD-quoted-pair shape
already validated by aura_v05321_alpaca_market_data.py's
discover_crypto_universe() (_USD_PAIR_RE) elsewhere in this codebase, so
this adapter now accepts the same discovered universe upstream can
actually produce a signal for -- not an unbounded "any string" symbol.
This adapter does not call Alpaca's own Assets API itself (it stays an
isolated, side-effect-free-by-default validator); Alpaca's order-
submission API remains the final live authority on whether a given
symbol is actually tradable, exactly as it already was for BTC/USD and
ETH/USD.

No other safety gate changes: kill_switch, execution_authorized,
paper_execution_authorized, live_execution, quantity, and client_order_id
validation are all untouched. TradingClient(..., paper=True) remains
mandatory and no live endpoint exists in this module.

The explicitly-superseded aura_v05322_alpaca_paper_execution.py draft
(marked SUPERSEDED in its own docstring, "kept as-is, still passing, for
history/reference") is deliberately left untouched.

Adds 4 cases to the existing subprocess-based contract test: a discovered
symbol beyond BTC/ETH (AVAX/USD) now validates, while a malformed symbol
and a non-USD-quoted pair still fail closed. All 11 cases in that file
pass. Full pytest suite (81 tests) green.

